en't enough air defense  systems to protect uh Ukraine because  it's such a big country it needs  airplanes so I hope zelinski I expect  him to bring that up with President  Biden and say come on we need more  airplanes in order to fight this and  also please help us with the emergency  assistance to keep our electrical grid  alive we don't know how many more  strikes uh the system can take before it  goes down  let's bring in Charles Stratford who  joins us live now from cave hello there  Charles this visit certainly signals the  importance of Ukraine's relationship  with the US doesn't it  it certainly does and of course it comes  at a critical time in the wake of these  weeks of missile and Kamikaze drone  strikes against ukrainian's vital energy  infrastructure more than a thousand we  understand  um in these recent weeks and uh yeah it  underscores the kind of Reliance that  zielinski um has on Western weapons on  Western support and the U.S in  particular we understand that this new  um this new arms package that is going  to be announced in Washington could be  another to worth another two billion  dollars that's already on top of a  commitment of what 18.5 billion dollars  from the US a lot of focus is going to  be on whether we're going to hear an  announcement finally about these Patriot  missile systems that the ukrainians have  been asking for for so long this has  been a hugely controversial subject um  previously the Biden Administration has  said no it wouldn't be sending this kind  of Weaponry because it was so Advanced  and there were fears it's understood  that this could be seen as an escalation  by Russia or an Escalade Moscow could  see it as an escalation and of course  there are huge challenges in using these  weapons they are very complex  um to use they involve a lot of training  some analysts say that Patriot missile  training can take up to a year we don't  know whether that training has started  certainly isn't in this country but  there 